        "original_id": "71ef6352-ce8b-5f8d-9a1d-f1578d6d69b2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Æthelweard, Æthelred I of Wessex, Alfred the Great, Cynric\n- Works: Anglo-Saxon Chronicle, Chronicon Æthelweardi, The Kine Saga\n- Roles: ealdorman\n- Topics: Anglo-Saxon history, Old English, name etymology\n\nFacts:\n- The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle is a collection of annals in Old English that chronicles the history of the Anglo-Saxons.\n- Everything known about Cynric comes from the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle.\n- Æthelweard, who died around 998, was descended from the Anglo-Saxon King Æthelred I of Wessex, the elder brother of Alfred the Great.\n- Æthelweard was an ealdorman and the author of a Latin version of the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle called the Chronicon Æthelweardi.\n- The name Kine in The Kine Saga comes from an Old English word for the weasel.",
